    "1": {
        "reproduce_code": "<!-- index.html -->\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n  <title>Carbon Modal Scroll-Lock Repro</title>\n  <!-- Carbon CSS -->\n  <link\n    rel=\"stylesheet\"\n    href=\"https://unpkg.com/carbon-components@10.3.2/css/carbon-components.min.css\"\n  />\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div id=\"root\"></div>\n\n  <!-- React and ReactDOM -->\n  <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/react@16/umd/react.development.js\"></script>\n  <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/react-dom@16/umd/react-dom.development.js\"></script>\n  <!-- Carbon Components React -->\n  <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/carbon-components-react@7.2.0/dist/carbon-components-react.min.js\"></script>\n  <script>\n    const {\n      ComposedModal,\n      ModalHeader,\n      ModalBody,\n      ModalFooter,\n      Button,\n    } = CarbonComponentsReact;\n\n    function App() {\n      const [open, setOpen] = React.useState(false);\n      return (\n        React.createElement('div', null,\n          React.createElement(Button, { onClick: () => setOpen(true) }, 'Show modal'),\n          React.createElement('div', {\n            style: {\n              height: '1500px',\n              backgroundColor: '#f4f4f4',\n              marginTop: '1rem',\n              padding: '1rem',\n            }\n          },\n            'Scroll this background content while the modal is open.'\n          ),\n          React.createElement(\n            ComposedModal,\n            {\n              open: open,\n              onRequestClose: () => setOpen(false),\n              onRequestSubmit: () => setOpen(false)\n            },\n            React.createElement(ModalHeader, {\n              title: 'Modal Title',\n              label: 'Optional Label'\n            }),\n            React.createElement(ModalBody, null,\n              'This is the modal content. Try scrolling the page\u2014background will continue to scroll.'\n            ),\n            React.createElement(ModalFooter, {\n              primaryButtonText: 'Save',\n              secondaryButtonText: 'Cancel'\n            })\n          )\n        )\n      );\n    }\n\n    ReactDOM.render(\n      React.createElement(App),\n      document.getElementById('root')\n    );\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>",
        "explanation": "This minimal example pulls in Carbon CSS and Carbon React from the CDN, renders a tall scrollable content area on the page, and places a ComposedModal that is controlled by React state. When you click the \u201cShow modal\u201d button, the modal opens but you can still scroll the background document. This reproduces the issue of the body (parent element) scrolling not being disabled when the modal is open.",
        "bug_scenario": "In Carbon Components React v7.2.0 (Carbon v10.3.2), when you open a Transactional/Passive modal (ComposedModal), the page behind the modal remains scrollable. In the provided GIF you can see that after clicking \u201cShow modal,\u201d you can still scroll the document body even though the modal is open\u2014there is no scroll lock on the background."
    }
}